    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327-a1">

                <pb facs="0641" n="581" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg581"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Señor Lerdo de Tejada to Mr. Plumb.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 11, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: have the honor to inform you that the
                    President of the republic having been pleased to appoint me minister of foreign
                    relations, I have taken charge to-day of that department.</p>
                <p>It is very satisfactory to me to assure you that I will always have the greatest
                    desire to cultivate the most friendly and cordial relations with the legation of
                    the United States of America, of which you are very worthily in charge. I am,
                    sir, with the greatest consideration, very respectfully, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. LERDO DE TEJADA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward Lee Plumb</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires of the United States of America,
                            in Mexico.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
